IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc29-xxviii-4-appeal-812`

-- ccc29-tests-xxviii-4-appeal-812.l4 -- tests for sections 812 to 828 of the Criminal Code (Canada).
-- Every expected value is written from the text before the run, beside its assertion. Argument order is the GIVEN order of each function.

§ `Tests -- section 812`

#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Ontario` EQUALS `s 812(1)(a) the Superior Court of Justice sitting in the region, district or county or group of counties where the adjudication was made`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Quebec` EQUALS `s 812(1)(b) the Superior Court`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Nova Scotia` EQUALS `s 812(1)(c) the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) British Columbia` EQUALS `s 812(1)(c) the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Prince Edward Island` EQUALS `s 812(1)(c) the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Newfoundland and Labrador` EQUALS `s 812(1)(c) the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) New Brunswick` EQUALS `s 812(1)(d) the Court of Queen's Bench`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Manitoba` EQUALS `s 812(1)(d) the Court of Queen's Bench`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Saskatchewan` EQUALS `s 812(1)(d) the Court of Queen's Bench`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Alberta` EQUALS `s 812(1)(d) the Court of Queen's Bench`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Yukon` EQUALS `s 812(1)(h) a judge of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) the Northwest Territories` EQUALS `s 812(1)(h) a judge of the Supreme Court`
#ASSERT `s 812(1) the appeal court for sections 813 to 828` `s 812(1) Nunavut` EQUALS `s 812(1)(i) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`
-- 812(2): a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut where the appeal is from a summary conviction court consisting of a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
#ASSERT `s 812(2) the appeal court once subsection (2) is applied` `s 812(1) Nunavut` TRUE EQUALS `s 812(2) a judge of the Court of Appeal of Nunavut`
#ASSERT `s 812(2) the appeal court once subsection (2) is applied` `s 812(1) Nunavut` FALSE EQUALS `s 812(1)(i) a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice`
#ASSERT `s 812(2) the appeal court once subsection (2) is applied` `s 812(1) Ontario` FALSE EQUALS `s 812(1)(a) the Superior Court of Justice sitting in the region, district or county or group of counties where the adjudication was made`

§ `Tests -- sections 813 to 815`

-- 813: (the appellant, the decision, the law otherwise provides, instituted at the instance of the Government of Canada).
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` `s 813 a conviction or order made against the defendant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` `s 813 a sentence passed on the defendant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` `s 813 a verdict of unfit to stand trial` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` `s 813 a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` `s 813 an order that dismisses an information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` `s 813 an order that stays proceedings on an information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` `s 813 another decision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the defendant in proceedings under this Part` `s 813 a conviction or order made against the defendant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the informant` `s 813 an order that stays proceedings on an information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the informant` `s 813 an order that dismisses an information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the informant` `s 813 a sentence passed on the defendant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the informant` `s 813 a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the informant` `s 813 a verdict of unfit to stand trial` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the informant` `s 813 a conviction or order made against the defendant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent` `s 813 an order that dismisses an information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the Attorney General or the Attorney General's agent` `s 813 another decision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of Canada's agent` `s 813 an order that dismisses an information` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 the Attorney General of Canada or the Attorney General of Canada's agent` `s 813 an order that dismisses an information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 813 the person may appeal to the appeal court` `s 813 another person` `s 813 a sentence passed on the defendant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 814: where the appeal is heard.
#ASSERT `s 814 the place at which the appeal under section 813 is required to be heard` `s 812(1) Manitoba` EQUALS JUST `s 814(1) the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the cause of the proceedings arose`
#ASSERT `s 814 the place at which the appeal under section 813 is required to be heard` `s 812(1) Alberta` EQUALS JUST `s 814(1) the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the cause of the proceedings arose`
#ASSERT `s 814 the place at which the appeal under section 813 is required to be heard` `s 812(1) Saskatchewan` EQUALS JUST `s 814(2) the sittings of the appeal court at the judicial centre nearest to the place where the adjudication was made`
#ASSERT `s 814 the place at which the appeal under section 813 is required to be heard` `s 812(1) British Columbia` EQUALS JUST `s 814(3) the sittings of the appeal court held nearest to the place where the adjudication was made`
#ASSERT `s 814 the place at which the appeal under section 813 is required to be heard` `s 812(1) Yukon` EQUALS JUST `s 814(4) the place where the cause of the proceedings arose or the place nearest to it where a court is appointed to be held`
#ASSERT `s 814 the place at which the appeal under section 813 is required to be heard` `s 812(1) Nunavut` EQUALS JUST `s 814(4) the place where the cause of the proceedings arose or the place nearest to it where a court is appointed to be held`
#ASSERT `s 814 the place at which the appeal under section 813 is required to be heard` `s 812(1) Ontario` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 814 the judge of the appeal court may appoint another place for the hearing of the appeal` `s 812(1) Manitoba` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 814 the judge of the appeal court may appoint another place for the hearing of the appeal` `s 812(1) Manitoba` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 814 the judge of the appeal court may appoint another place for the hearing of the appeal` `s 812(1) British Columbia` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 814 the judge of the appeal court may appoint another place for the hearing of the appeal` `s 812(1) Nunavut` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 814 the judge of the appeal court may appoint another place for the hearing of the appeal` `s 812(1) Ontario` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 815.
#ASSERT `s 815(1) the appellant is required to give notice of appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 815(1) the appellant is required to give notice of appeal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 815(1) the notice of appeal is given within the period directed by the rules of court` 30 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 815(1) the notice of appeal is given within the period directed by the rules of court` 31 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 815(2) the appeal court or a judge thereof may extend the time within which notice of appeal may be given` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 815(2) the appeal court or a judge thereof may extend the time within which notice of appeal may be given` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- sections 816 to 820`

-- 816(1): (defendant-appellant, in custody, the appeal court makes a release order).
#ASSERT `s 816(1) the appellant is required to remain in custody` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 816(1) the appellant is required to remain in custody` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 816(1) the appellant is required to remain in custody` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 816(1) the appellant is required to remain in custody` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
