#ASSERT `s 817(1) the justice is required to order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 817(1) the justice is required to order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 817(2) the condition of the recognizance is that the prosecutor will appear personally or by counsel at the sittings of the appeal court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 817(2) the condition of the recognizance is that the prosecutor will appear personally or by counsel at the sittings of the appeal court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 817(3) section 817 does not apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 817(3) section 817 does not apply` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 818(1): (a justice makes an order under 817, the person is the appellant or the respondent, the application is made before or during the hearing).
#ASSERT `s 818(1) the appellant or the respondent may apply to the appeal court for a review of the order made by the justice` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 818(1) the appellant or the respondent may apply to the appeal court for a review of the order made by the justice` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 818(1) the appellant or the respondent may apply to the appeal court for a review of the order made by the justice` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 818(1) the appellant or the respondent may apply to the appeal court for a review of the order made by the justice` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
