#ASSERT `s 828(1) the conviction or order may be enforced in the way` TRUE `s 828(1)(a) in the same manner as if it had been made by the summary conviction court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 828(1) the conviction or order may be enforced in the way` TRUE `s 828(1)(b) by process of the appeal court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 828(1) the conviction or order may be enforced in the way` TRUE `s 828(1) another way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 828(1) the conviction or order may be enforced in the way` FALSE `s 828(1)(a) in the same manner as if it had been made by the summary conviction court` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 828(2) the summary conviction court or a justice may issue a warrant of committal as if no appeal had been taken` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 828(2) the summary conviction court or a justice may issue a warrant of committal as if no appeal had been taken` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 828(2) the summary conviction court or a justice may issue a warrant of committal as if no appeal had been taken` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` TRUE `s 828(3) the conviction or order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` TRUE `s 828(3) a writing relating to the conviction or order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` TRUE `s 828(3) the notice of intention to appeal` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` TRUE `s 828(3) an undertaking` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` TRUE `s 828(3) a release order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` TRUE `s 828(3) a recognizance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` TRUE `s 828(3) a document that does not relate to the conviction or order` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is required to send the document to the justice` FALSE `s 828(3) the conviction or order` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Regulative rules -- sections 815 to 828`

#TRACE `s 815(1) the appellant is to give notice of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 815 the appellant` DOES `s 815(1) give notice of appeal` AT 1
#TRACE `s 816(1.1) the custodian is to release the appellant` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `s 816(1.1) release the appellant` AT 0
#TRACE `s 817(1) the prosecutor is to appear before a justice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 817(1) appear before a justice` AT 0
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 817(1) order that the prosecutor enter into a recognizance` AT 3
#TRACE `s 819(1) the custodian is to apply to the appeal court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `s 819(1) apply to the appeal court to fix a date for the hearing of the appeal` AT 0
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 819(2) fix a date for the hearing of the appeal and give directions for expediting the hearing` AT 5
#TRACE `s 821(1) the clerk is to notify the summary conviction court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the clerk of the court` DOES `s 821(1) notify the summary conviction court of the appeal` AT 1
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 821(1) transmit the conviction, order or order of dismissal and all other material to the appeal court` AT 4
#TRACE `s 828(3) the clerk of the appeal court is to send the conviction or order to the justice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the clerk of the court` DOES `s 828(3) send the conviction or order and the writings relating to it to the justice` AT 1

-- Breach paths. Only the three rules that carry a deadline can be driven to BREACH: "immediately", "immediately after filing" and "forthwith" are WITHIN 0 days, so the same event one day later breaches.
-- A rule with no WITHIN reads FULFILLED for a late event and leaves an event by another party unmatched (probed on s 800(1) on both builds), so no trace is written for those.
#TRACE `s 816(1.1) the custodian is to release the appellant` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `s 816(1.1) release the appellant` AT 1
#TRACE `s 817(1) the prosecutor is to appear before a justice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 817(1) appear before a justice` AT 1
#TRACE `s 819(1) the custodian is to apply to the appeal court` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `s 819(1) apply to the appeal court to fix a date for the hearing of the appeal` AT 1
